  "short_description": "",
  "description": "<p data-start=\"16\" data-end=\"76\">Sometimes a pedal setup needs just a little extra clearance.</p>\n<p data-start=\"78\" data-end=\"450\">Barefoot Buttons Spacers are designed to raise the button slightly when a switch head is too short for the set screws to fully secure against, or when additional height clearance is needed around LED rings or recessed switch areas. Installed inside the bore of the button, the spacer lifts the button approximately 1/16&#8243; to help create a more secure and reliable fit.</p>\n<p data-start=\"452\" data-end=\"595\">Simple, effective, and easy to install, Spacer Rings can help solve compatibility and clearance issues without changing the feel of your setup.</p>\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1d7mrtu\" data-start=\"597\" data-end=\"608\">Features</h2>\n<ul data-start=\"610\" data-end=\"867\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1q6pmio\" data-start=\"610\" data-end=\"652\">Raises button height approximately 1/16&#8243;</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1vlk6me\" data-start=\"653\" data-end=\"696\">Helps improve fit on shorter switch heads</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1oft9kn\" data-start=\"697\" data-end=\"757\">Useful for pedals with LED rings or tight switch clearance</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1e6jpvn\" data-start=\"758\" data-end=\"798\">Installs inside the bore of the button</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1pxehia\" data-start=\"799\" data-end=\"828\">Lightweight and low profile</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"id91tq\" data-start=\"829\" data-end=\"867\">Compatible with V1 and Big Bore fits</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-section-id=\"14bu82z\" data-start=\"869\" data-end=\"885\">Compatibility</h2>\n<p data-start=\"887\" data-end=\"903\">Compatible with:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"904\" data-end=\"953\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1j6dg7g\" data-start=\"904\" data-end=\"925\">V1 Barefoot Buttons</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"swr7nh\" data-start=\"926\" data-end=\"953\">Big Bore Barefoot Buttons</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"955\" data-end=\"975\">Not compatible with:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"976\" data-end=\"991\">\n<li data-section-id=\"yhmu8c\" data-start=\"976\" data-end=\"980\">V2</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"11gv406\" data-start=\"981\" data-end=\"991\">Max Bore</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1vgjuc7\" data-start=\"993\" data-end=\"1024\">Why Players Use Spacers</h2>\n<p data-start=\"1026\" data-end=\"1313\">Not every pedal switch is built exactly the same. Some switches sit lower, have shorter heads, or include LED housings that reduce clearance around the button. Spacers provide a simple way to fine tune fitment while keeping the clean look and control Barefoot Buttons are known for.</p>\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1p3u389\" data-start=\"1315\" data-end=\"1330\">Installation</h2>\n<p data-start=\"1332\" data-end=\"1533\">Place the Spacers inside the bore of the Barefoot Button before installing onto the switch. Once installed, the spacer slightly raises the button to improve set screw contact and overall clearance.</p>\n<h2 data-section-id=\"ntyisd\" data-start=\"1535\" data-end=\"1546\">Included</h2>\n<ul data-start=\"1548\" data-end=\"1603\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1efusme\" data-start=\"1548\" data-end=\"1603\" data-is-last-node=\"\">4 spacers</li>\n</ul>",
